Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: rg35xx-2024: keep the RAM voltage the SPL set

The RG35XX 2024 device tree, which the Plus, H and SP include, pins vdd-dram at
1.1V for LPDDR4, but these devices are also sold with LPDDR3, which runs at
1.2V (an SP has it). The SPL finds out which one the unit has and sets the
voltage for it. With a range of 1.1V to 1.2V, Linux leaves the regulator where
it is, since it only moves a voltage outside the range, so it neither
undervolts LPDDR3 nor overvolts LPDDR4.
ROCKNIX instead sets 1.2V through its H700 ddr3 overlay, in its LPDDR3 build.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-2024.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-2024.dts
index 15dbb4b3..aaa398f3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-2024.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-2024.dts
@@ -473,3 +473,12 @@
 &pwm {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * LPDDR4 runs at 1.1V and LPDDR3 at 1.2V. The SPL tries both and sets the
+ * voltage of the one that works; Linux keeps it, as it is inside this range.
+ */
+&reg_dcdc3 {
+	regulator-min-microvolt = <1100000>;
+	regulator-max-microvolt = <1200000>;
+};
